{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1377651-doing-a-technocracy-game-looking-for-inspiration","id":1377651,"title":"doing a technocracy game. looking for inspiration","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-31T22:03:23-07:00","id":1377651,"title":"doing a technocracy game. looking for inspiration","content":"set in present day North America. <br /> <br /> four out of five conventions represented, not sure which yet but four players and an npc to round out the team. <br /> <br /> definitely an iterator tech blogger, a syndicate wolf of wall street with a heart of gold who wants financial stability for all. <br /> <br /> the other two are undecided<br /> <br /> one is going for a raw recruit who has no convention, this is a toughie for me, they know nothing about the technocracy and are wanting to play a 'neonate' mage (they come from vampire) and I don't really know how to play it. <br /> <br /> last player is undecided entirely, we'll see what he takes. <br /> <br /> I NEED IDEAS<br /> <br /> where should this chronicle go, what do the players need to see and feel, I mean all that is very much determined by what their needs are and you won't know that but generally im just searching for ideas. <br /> <br /> they don't want a hunters game (so no killing vampires and garou, at least not indiscriminately), there's a soft peace with the traditions, the internal conflict in the is union cooled down but still there, and the nephandi are deemed more of a threat now and both sides (trads and union) can agree on that. <br /> <br /> its 2020, so everything in the revised con books is cannon but old now, hence the changes above. <br /> <br /> <br /> any ideas are welcome, just looking for places to take the chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-31T22:22:28-07:00","id":1377653,"title":"","content":"What part of North America? And what sort of game they expressed interest in (action, political intrigue, mystery, conspiracy, horror, etc.)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-31T22:24:40-07:00","id":1377654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1377651-doing-a-technocracy-game-looking-for-inspiration?p=1377653#post1377653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What part of North America? And what sort of game they expressed interest in (action, political intrigue, mystery, conspiracy, horror, etc.)?</div> </div> </div> </div>probably vancouver. maybe somewhere else. a major city in all likelihood. <br /> <br /> as for interests expressed, not much has been said, they're all new to mage or at least the union, so the real interest grabber is that its new and shiny and ive wanted to do a union game for ages","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-31T22:33:18-07:00","id":1377657,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Some sort of investigation that eventually leads to Seattle's aerospace industry, maybe? And then perhaps further down the coast to Silicon Valley, and eventually to something in LA or Vegas?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-31T22:37:41-07:00","id":1377659,"title":"","content":"You could try making it about revising the Technocracy, to weed out the corruption, or failing that them branching out to make a more idealized less Our Way or the Highway splinter group of Technocrats.<br /> <br /> Or hunt down the societal predators of the Reality Deviants, start with the Hematavores who are manipulating the stock market through their pawns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-31T23:13:18-07:00","id":1377664,"title":"","content":"There are just so many directions you can go. <br /> <br /> I forget what book it was in; but there was a mage supplement that listed a bunch of movie inspirations organized by Tradition and Convention. It's very much out of date by now; but I'd still suggest showing something like that to the players to give them some ideas of what kinds of stories a Technocracy game might entail. <br /> <br /> I don't really see \u201cneonate who hasn't chosen a Convention yet\u201d as a viable option; despite all their talk about unity, the Technocracy just doesn't work that way, any more than the Traditions do. There simply isn't a \u201cgeneric Technocrat\u201d. <br /> <br /> One possibility you might consider would be an ex-Etherite \u2014 one of the less bizarre ones, but one who was something of a jack of all trades compared to the more specialized training that Technocrats tend to have. (S)he has already been processed into the Union, which wasn't hard because of the aforementioned lack of radical divergence from Conventional Science; but no decision has yet been made as to which Convention (s)he will join. I'd say they (s)he used to be an Adventurer, and is quite well-versed in the science of combat (your team so far doesn't seem to have a combat specialist), and could potentially end up in any Convention's fighting forces.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-31T23:26:15-07:00","id":1377668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1377651-doing-a-technocracy-game-looking-for-inspiration?p=1377664#post1377664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I forget what book it was in; but there was a mage supplement that listed a bunch of movie inspirations organized by Tradition and Convention. It's very much out of date by now; but I'd still suggest showing something like that to the players to give them some ideas of what kinds of stories a Technocracy game might entail.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> storyteller's handbook revised. and good call DW","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T00:34:57-07:00","id":1377678,"title":"","content":"As far as movies as potential plots, Three Days of the Condor makes a great Technocrat one. It's a 1975 film with Robert Redford as a CIA analyst who comes back from lunch to find all his coworkers murdered, and has to go on the run trusting no one while he tries to find out who did it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T03:31:09-07:00","id":1377701,"title":"","content":"Guide to the Technocracy gave me some cool inspirations alongside Tales of Dark Magick. A little unrelated, but I found the video game FEAR was a really good inspiration you can base an entire chronicle on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26024-distant-choir","name":"Distant Choir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26024_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T21:46:45-07:00","id":1378470,"title":"","content":"If you can track down the movie Gog, it's on Amazon prime. It's the perfect plot for a technocrat game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T08:55:16-07:00","id":1378770,"title":"","content":"From my (limited) understanding, the Nephandi are not usually monstrous demons wanting to brawl across the city. More like the nice guy behind the counter who can &quot;get you want you need if you would only do him this little favor&quot;. <br /> <br /> And because &quot;after all, you need it; they don't&quot;. <br /> &quot;Shouldn't you get what you deserve, after all that hard work you put into it?&quot;. <br /> &quot;Its really yours, after all. You worked for it, sweated for it, bled for it, and it was just handed to them. Is that really owning it?&quot;<br /> &quot;Me, oh no, I can't give you anything. I can only guide your to earn that power for yourself.&quot;<br /> &quot;Its not a bargain. You don't lose anything. Its not that you are trading something of yourself. I am just showing you what you need to do to unlock your natural power.&quot;<br /> &quot;Oh dear, that didn't go like you planned. But that's okay, mistakes happen. I know of a fix you can do to make everything all better...&quot;<br /> <br /> So there a lot of room for not only struggling against corrupted people, but against being corrupted one's self.<br /> <br /> Other monsters exist, as well. The Void Engineers can't keep every beast out of reality, and some one needs to deal with them once they get in. <br /> <br /> Human monsters can be interesting. Serial killers, kidnappers, etc. Add in trying to figure out why the great machine of Reality allows such terrible people to exist is an idea.<br /> <br /> What if, some how, a human mundane learns how to manipulate the stock markets better than a syndicate member? What if this human is using the money to fund terrorism?<br /> <br /> Every organization has its bad apples. Who is the bad apples in your setting? Can they be stopped?<br /> <br /> Another idea is a massive spirit running/is the city, and its beginning to die. It can be so massive no one can see it (ants on a beach ball), yet the city is breaking down. How can the Technocrats fix it? Do they replace it with another massive spirit, or use a swarm of smaller spirits? Can they make a machine made of spirits to do its job? Should they let the city die?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3097-gator-the-unread","name":"Gator the Unread","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T15:40:02-07:00","id":1378859,"title":"","content":"Honestly, the best way, IMO to run a Technocracy game isn't to focus on it like you're part of the military.<br /> <br /> You're cops. Magic Cops.<br /> <br /> Maybe there's a murder that the local police wrote off as gang violence, but one of the Unions Plants on the police force found a runic talisman duct-taped under their desk and flagged the case for Union review.<br /> <br /> Stuff like that. Typical detective/cop stuff only you're tracking down magic crime. You're not dropping traditionalists just for being traditionalists... But there's probably still some friction there. Neither side likes the other. And when some Euthanatos nut goes and starts executing city officials in a series of impossible murders... Well. Crime is crime. Murder is murder.<br /> <br /> Maybe throw in a few rogue agents as well, alongside some potentially grudgingly friendly traditionalists to muddy the waters further.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T16:10:10-07:00","id":1378870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1377651-doing-a-technocracy-game-looking-for-inspiration?p=1378859#post1378859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, the best way, IMO to run a Technocracy game isn't to focus on it like you're part of the military.<br /> <br /> You're cops. Magic Cops.<br /> <br /> Maybe there's a murder that the local police wrote off as gang violence, but one of the Unions Plants on the police force found a runic talisman duct-taped under their desk and flagged the case for Union review.<br /> <br /> Stuff like that. Typical detective/cop stuff only you're tracking down magic crime. You're not dropping traditionalists just for being traditionalists... But there's probably still some friction there. Neither side likes the other. And when some Euthanatos nut goes and starts executing city officials in a series of impossible murders... Well. Crime is crime. Murder is murder.<br /> <br /> Maybe throw in a few rogue agents as well, alongside some potentially grudgingly friendly traditionalists to muddy the waters further.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like it. very cool. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T07:47:08-07:00","id":1379251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zennis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1377651-doing-a-technocracy-game-looking-for-inspiration#post1377651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> definitely an iterator tech blogger, a syndicate wolf of wall street with a heart of gold who wants financial stability for all.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div> Sit down with your players and talk to them about, what they want to do with their characters in game and how they want to do it. The limiting aspects your focus can have on Magick are hard for many new(and old) players to grasp. And those aspects are even more limiting for Technocrats.<br /> A cybernetically enhanced Iteration X with who uses and builds a lot of hypertech has a lot more room as to what she can do with enlightened Science then a tech blogger.<br /> And the Syndicate has one of the most challenging approaches to enlightened Science in the hands of a player. Because it is real subtle and behind the scene long term stuff. I have seen awful stuff happen with Syndicate Mages in players hands. Syndicate Banker sounds nice on paper. But in game the player probably wants to go out and have an adventure with the rest of the gang and not sit in his boardroom all day subtly influence markets, allocate resources and send those and backup to the rest of the players.( It's not that I can't see that working, it's just that in my experience it is not the way in which most players want to engage in a game)<br /> <br /> Generally think about how important theme and tone are for you in the game. A lot of Technocrat games that I have seen online and offline have Technocrats basically using enlightened Science like Reality Deviants would use Magick, because players, especially if they are new to mage, are, understandably, not very good at \u201cthe Sphere rating says I can do that, but my character would never do it like that\u201d.<br /> <br /> If theme and tone aren't important to you and you just want to run a fun Technocrat game, none of the above is important.<br /> <br /> But otherwise think/talk about that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25507-nobby","name":"nobby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25507_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T16:16:17-07:00","id":1380511,"title":"","content":"I think a good source of inspiration for this sort of low key behind the scenes technomancy game would be an old show I used to watch called Person of Interest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/706-rickayelm","name":"rickayelm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T00:24:20-07:00","id":1380592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rickayelm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1377651-doing-a-technocracy-game-looking-for-inspiration?p=1380511#post1380511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a good source of inspiration for this sort of low key behind the scenes technomancy game would be an old show I used to watch called Person of Interest.</div> </div> </div> </div>tell me about it<br /> what's your take on it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T11:49:00-07:00","id":1380718,"title":"","content":"It's a show about a computer programmer who becomes a billionaire because of his advanced creations. Before the show starts he creates an ai to help the government hunt terrorist after 9/11, but the AI starts finding all sorts of crimes that the NSA aren't interested so he recruits other people to help him fight crime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/706-rickayelm","name":"rickayelm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T20:34:31-07:00","id":1381202,"title":"","content":"Look up SCP (Special Containment Protocols) Foundation on YouTube. These stories were MADE to be converted into a Technocracy game. Seriously, this basically IS the Technocracy, but in another World of Darkness. <br /> <br /> Here are a few good ones that you can use as inspiration for the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/9Z0YMJUaNrw\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/9Z0YMJUaNrw\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/9Z0YMJUaNrw\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/9Z0YMJUaNrw </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/F2ZwAUzABZE\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/F2ZwAUzABZE\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/F2ZwAUzABZE\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/F2ZwAUzABZE </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/vVI3EGsfoqU\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/vVI3EGsfoqU\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/vVI3EGsfoqU\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/vVI3EGsfoqU </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/qA66U34zM6c\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/qA66U34zM6c\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/qA66U34zM6c\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/qA66U34zM6c </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/-q1P768F-EA\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/-q1P768F-EA\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/-q1P768F-EA\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/-q1P768F-EA </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 04-13-2020, 11:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T13:52:07-07:00","id":1381761,"title":"","content":"I always thought that Warehouse 13 (or the GURPS sourcebook/set up that preceded it, Warehouse 23) made for an interesting potential Technocracy set up. A team that's responsible for going out and recovering dangerous reality bending/breaking artifacts and locking them up for safe keeping.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T14:35:49-07:00","id":1381765,"title":"","content":"I think most of what any Technocracy game needs is simply to reskin common WoD tropes with new nomeclature and look at things from that different perspective. A Lovecraftian/Cosmicism perspective would be the best to promote the Technocracy as being the good guys. Instead of a Gauntlet and an Umbra, they say reality is sitting on a dimensional fault line and when there's a disturbance, horrible things can come through. It's their job to repair that faultline and eliminate the monstrosities that come through. Magic and similar stuff is bad because it weakens that faultline.<br /> <br /> I think key elements would include exploration (finding new phenomenon), identification (research of the newly found phenomenon), and containment (elimination, retrieval, or safe storage of the phenomenon). Phenomenon might include people, places, or objects.<br /> <br /> I would divide things into &quot;Monsters of the Week&quot; (unrelated phenomenon, but fun to showcase reskinned standard WoD elements and new ideas), and some kind of chronicle tentpole (various scenarios linked to a common phenomenon).<br /> <br /> I agree with Mercurial that there's a lot of good things you can find in the SCP Foundation as inspiration. Materials for Delta Green/Call of Cthulhu can also be reskinned. The great thing about these games, is that unlike many RPGs, the bulk of published material isn't about settings, but scenarios so you can find lots of stuff (it does take work to reskin things, but much less than coming up with your own. Spend less time trying to mechanically match things, and more on determining the core aspects of the adventure and replacing their monsters with WoD style creatures you like).<br /> <br /> A possible tentpole idea is exploring an &quot;alternate dimension&quot; adjacent to Earth, which might be a Penumbral Domain to Malfeas, or a Near Realm. This <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/setting-riff-voices-from-below-and-the-long-stairs.391379/\" target=\"_blank\">old thread from RPG.Net </a>has some neat ideas on how the exploration might go. Very much like a Stargate style kind of exploration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T17:01:27-07:00","id":1381811,"title":"","content":"So lean heavily on the Void Engineers. Yeah; that can work. (Stargate, in particular, provides a reasonable VE-themed Technocracy game without needing much in the way of Voidships.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}